#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_finite_field_element_primitive

#% text
# `is_finite_field_element_primitive(a)` gives `true` when the finite field element `a` generates the multiplicative group of its field, and `false` otherwise.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The test checks `a^((q - 1)/r) != 1` for every prime `r` dividing `q - 1`; when `q - 1` cannot be factored the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
F = finite_field(7, 2)

#% cell
is_finite_field_element_primitive(F([0, 1]))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_finite_field_element_primitive(F([0, 1])^2)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# There are `euler_phi(q - 1)` primitive elements:

#% cell
[count(table(is_finite_field_element_primitive(F(k)), k, range(1, 48)), true), euler_phi(48)]
#% output
#= [16, 16]

